cinschi","from_t":1997.0383561643835,"to_t":2001.2630136986302,"title":"President of Moldova","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Petru Lucinschi"},{"qid":"Q217","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q4164146","value_label":"Igor Dodon","from_t":2016.9754098360656,"to_t":2020.9781420765028,"title":"President of Moldova","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Igor Dodon"},{"qid":"Q217","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q57478","value_label":"Nicolae Timofti","from_t":2012.22131147541,"to_t":2016.9754098360656,"title":"President of Moldova","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Nicolae Timofti"},{"qid":"Q217","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q57685","value_label":"Vlad Filat","from_t":2010.9890410958903,"to_t":2010.9945205479453,"title":"President of Moldova","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Vlad Filat"},{"qid":"Q217","kind":"flag","value_qid":"Q167584","value_label":"Flag of Moldova.svg","from_t":1990.8465753424657,"to_t":null,"title":"flag of Moldova","property":"P163","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"flag of Moldova"}],"people":{"Q15071069":{"label":"Maia Sandu","description":"President of Moldova since 2020","enwiki":"Maia Sandu","summary":"Maia Sandu (Romanian: [ˈmaja ˈsandu]; born 24 May 1972) is a Moldovan politician and economist who, since 2020, has served as the sixth president of Moldova. She is the founder and former leader of the Party of Action and Solidarity (PAS) and was prime minister of Moldova from June to November 2019, when her government collapsed after a vote of no-confidence. Sandu was minister of education from 2012 to 2015 and member of the parliament of Moldova from 2014 to 2015, and again in 2019.\nSandu was elected president of Moldova during the 2020 Moldovan presidential election.","image":"Maia Sandu, September 2025.jpg","birth":1972.3934426229507,"death":null},"Q140480413":{"label":"Vasile Tofan","description":"Moldovan investor and businessman (born 1982), Prime Minister of Moldova","enwiki":"Vasile Tofan","summary":"Vasile Tofan (born 12 July 1982) is a Moldovan investor and businessman. He has served as Prime Minister of Moldova since 22 July 2026, having been nominated by president Maia Sandu on 11 July.","image":"Vasile Tofan official portrait (cropped).jpg","birth":1982.5260273972603,"death":null},"Q189435":{"label":"Vladimir Voronin","description":"Moldovan politician, former President of Moldova","enwiki":"Vladimir Voronin","summary":"Vladimir Voronin (Romanian: [vladiˈmir voˈronin]; born Vladimir Bujeniță,  25 May 1941) is a Moldovan politician. He was the third President of Moldova from 2001 until 2009 and served as the leader of the Party of Communists of Moldova (PCRM) from 1994 until 2026. He was Europe's first democratically elected communist party head of state after the dissolution of the Eastern Bloc.","image":"Vladimir VORONIN, Fracțiunea parlamentară a Partidului Comuniștilor din Republica Moldova.jpg","birth":1941.3945205479451,"death":null},"Q294473":{"label":"Mihai Ghimpu","description":"Moldovan politician","enwiki":"Mihai Ghimpu","summary":"Mihai Ghimpu (born 19 November 1951) is a Moldovan politician who served as President of the Moldovan Parliament and Acting President of Moldova from 2009 to 2010. He was member of Parliament of Moldova from 1990 to 1998 and from 2009 to 2019. Ghimpu held the position of leader of Liberal Party (PL) from 1998 to 2018.","image":"Mihai Ghimpu Imagine.jpg","birth":1951.8821917808218,"death":null},"Q312340":{"label":"Marian Lupu","description":"Moldovan politician","enwiki":"Marian Lupu","summary":"Marian Lupu (Romanian: [mariˈan ˈlupu]; born 20 June 1966) is a Moldovan economist and politician who was the President of the Parliament of Moldova between 2010 and 2013. From this position he served as Acting President of Moldova from 2010 until 2012.\nHe was the president of the party Respect Moldova Movement (MRM) from 2025 to 2026, resigning following the party review of the 2025 Moldovan parliamentary election.","image":"Marian Lupu Senate of Poland.JPG","birth":1966.4657534246576,"death":null},"Q347679":{"label":"Mircea Snegur","description":"Moldovan politician","enwiki":"Mircea Snegur","summary":"Mircea Snegur (Romanian: [ˈmirtʃe̯a ˈsneɡur]; 17 January 1940 – 13 September 2023) was a Moldovan agronomist and politician who served as the first President of Moldova from 1990 to 1997. Prior to that, he served as the Chairman of the Presidium of the Supreme Soviet of the Moldavian SSR from 1989 to 1990 and chairman of the Supreme Soviet from 27 April to 3 September 1990.","image":"Mircea Snegur 1996 (cropped).jpg","birth":1940.0437158469945,"death":2023.6986301369864},"Q355874":{"label":"Petru Lucinschi","description":"Moldovan politician (born 1940)","enwiki":"Petru Lucinschi","summary":"Petru Lucinschi (Romanian: [ˈpetru luˈtʃinski]; born 27 January 1940) is a former Moldovan politician who was Moldova's second President from 1997 to 2001. He currently serves as the founder and head of the Lucinschi Foundation of Strategic Studies and International Relations.","image":"Первый награждённый почётным знаком СНГ.jpg","birth":1940.0710382513662,"death":null},"Q4164146":{"label":"Igor Dodon","description":"5th President of Moldova from 2016 until 2020","enwiki":"Igor Dodon","summary":"Igor Dodon (Romanian: [ˈiɡor doˈdon]; born 18 February 1975) is a Moldovan economist and politician who served as the 5th president of Moldova from 2016 to 2020. He currently serves as the leader of the Party of Socialists of the Republic of Moldova since 2024. He served as Minister of Economy and Trade in the governments of Vasile Tarlev and Zinaida Greceanîi from September 2006 to September 2009 and was a member of the Parliament of Moldova from 2009 to 2016. He lost his bid for re-election in 2020 to Maia Sandu, whom he had defeated four years earlier in the 2016 Moldovan presidential election.","image":"Igor DODON, Fracțiunea parlamentară a Partidului Socialiștilor din Republica Moldova.jpg","birth":1975.131506849315,"death":null},"Q57478":{"label":"Nicolae Timofti","description":"4th President of Moldova (r. 2012–2016)","enwiki":"Nicolae Timofti","summary":"Nicolae Timofti (Romanian: [nikoˈla.e tiˈmofti]; born 22 December 1948) is a Moldovan jurist and politician who was President of Moldova from 23 March 2012 until 23 December 2016. He served as head of Moldova's Superior Magistrate Council and was elected President by parliament on 16 March 2012.","image":"Nicolae Timofti.jpg","birth":1948.9726775956285,"death":null},"Q57685":{"label":"Vlad Filat","description":"Moldovan politician","enwiki":"Vlad Filat","summary":"Vladimir Filat (born 6 May 1969), commonly referred to as Vlad Filat (Romanian: [ˈvlad fiˈlat]), is a Moldovan businessman, politician, \nand tycoon and founder of Liberal Democratic Party of Moldova. He was Prime Minister of Moldova from 25 September 2009 to 25 April 2013. He also was appointed as the interim president of Moldova for a brief period of time in 2010.\nFollowing his conviction on charges of accepting bribes, Filat was released from jail in December 2019, 6 years earlier than his initial sentence.","image":"Vladimir Filat.jpg","birth":1969.3424657534247,"death":null}},"media":{"Flag of Moldova.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Flag_of_Moldova.svg/330px-Flag_of_Moldova.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Moldova.svg","author":"Gheorghe Vrabie","license":"Public domain"},"Coat of arms of Moldova.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Coat_of_arms_of_Moldova.svg/330px-Coat_of_arms_of_Moldova.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Moldova.svg","author":null,"license":"Public domain"},"Maia Sandu, September 2025.jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip